{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to question fa158c05 (BR-3 validation plan).\n\nAccepted: one instrumented ordinary `npm run gate` at the settled review\ncandidate, with VITEST_MAX_WORKERS unset and the project at two workers,\nserves as both the measurement run and the ordinary gate pass. Do not run\nscripts/measure-tests.sh, and do not run the native phase twice.\n\n\"Before\" figures: use the BR-9 ordinary gate at f4735c54 (one worker,\npassed, pre-R7 code) as the before run for every phase, and the R7 native\ncontinuation at ae49c5a6 (one worker, failed run, 778/2/2) as a second\nbefore point for the native phase only. Label each figure by how it was\ntaken (observed run; one worker; code head; uncontrolled load) and keep\nthe failed run labelled failed. Report phase times per stage of\nscripts/test.mjs for before and after, in one table, with the raw logs in\nthe evidence directory. No controlled speedup claim is needed; the\nacceptance asks for the phase times, not a ratio.\n\nIf the two-worker gate fails on shared-state tests, that is the \"medium\"\ncase in BR-3: repair, then one more ordinary gate at the new head, and\nthe failed run stays in the note as a separate outcome.","body":{"to":"builder"}}